  "question": {
    "text": "A tank with a small hole at the bottom has been filled with water and kerosene (specific gravity $0.8$ ). The height of water is $3 \\mathrm{~m}$ and that of kerosene $2 \\mathrm{~m}$. When the hole is opened the velocity of fluid coming out from it is nearly: (take $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-2}$ and density of water $\\left.=10^3 \\mathrm{~kg} \\mathrm{~m}^{-3}\\right)$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$10.7 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$9.6 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$8.5 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$7.6 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&h_1 \\rho_1 g+h_2 \\rho_2 g=\\frac{1}{2} \\rho_1 \\mathrm{v}^2 \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow 1000 \\times 10 \\times 3+800 \\times 10 \\times 2 \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2} \\times 1000 \\times \\mathrm{v}^2 \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{v}^2=2 \\times \\frac{46000}{1000} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{v}=\\sqrt{92}=9.6 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}